# API Gateway behaviour checks — HAND-WRITTEN (not generated), httpyac-specific
# (`??` assertions). Run post-deploy by `task smoke URL=<invoke url> ENV=<env>`
# against a real stage: these behaviours are produced by API Gateway in front
# of the Lambda (authorizer, gateway responses, CORS, API keys), so the local
# stub server cannot exercise them. No Cognito user is needed: every request
# here is expected to be REJECTED (or is public), which is exactly what proves
# the edge is configured.

### health — public liveness probe, no auth, no API key
# @name gateway_health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

?? status == 200
?? header content-type includes application/json
?? js response.parsedBody.status === "ok"

### no token → the Cognito authorizer rejects with the contract's problem+json and CORS
# @name gateway_unauthenticated
GET {{baseUrl}}/todos
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

?? status == 401
?? header content-type includes application/problem+json
?? header access-control-allow-origin exists
?? js response.parsedBody.status === 401
?? js typeof response.parsedBody.request_id === "string"

### garbage token → 401, not 500 and not a bare gateway message
# @name gateway_invalid_token
GET {{baseUrl}}/todos
Authorization: Bearer not-a-jwt
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

?? status == 401
?? header content-type includes application/problem+json

### unknown route → gateway response, still problem+json
# @name gateway_unknown_route
GET {{baseUrl}}/nope
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}

?? status in [401, 403, 404]
?? header content-type includes application/problem+json

### CORS preflight answered by the mock integration with the allow-list
# @name gateway_preflight
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/todos
Origin: https://app.example.com
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST

?? status == 204
?? header access-control-allow-origin exists
?? header access-control-allow-methods includes POST
?? header access-control-allow-headers includes idempotency-key
